<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">B. P. Koirala</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1914–1982</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Bishweshwar Prasad Koirala</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">B. P. Koirala (1914–1982) was a leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepali-congress">Nepali Congress</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a>'s first democratically elected prime minister, taking office in 1959. In December 1960 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahendra-of-nepal">King Mahendra</a> dismissed his government and imprisoned him, introducing the partyless panchayat system. After years in prison and exile he returned in 1976 to campaign for democracy, and he was also an important writer of Nepali fiction.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/b-p-koirala.jpg" alt="B. P. Koirala" width="320" height="389" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BP_Koirala.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
